<title>UK: BAA director takes profit on share options.</title>
<headline>BAA director takes profit on share options.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British airports operator BAA Plc's technical director Michael Maine exercised options on 91,150 shares in the company on Wednesday and sold them for a gross profit of 144,974.7 stg.</p>
<p>BAA said in a routine notice to the London Stock Exchange that Maine acquired 17,600 shares at 3.38 stg a share, 57,890 shares at 3.09 stg and a further 15,660 shares at 3.565 stg, and sold them all at 4.81 stg a share.</p>
<p>His remaining holding comprises 19,602 shares plus options on a further 70,354 shares, the company said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
